Z||000000||Lizzy||12-27-2001||02:43 PM||||When I start my Fiero, w/duke 4 cyl., it idles high and all is well.  As i give it some throttle the engine revs but then drops 500rpms.  It goes back and forth like this when i'm giving it some gas.  It idles fine.  After 2-3 minutes of warmup it goes away.  I've checked and no codes have come up, so i've replaced the map sensor and that was not the problem.  Any help would be appreciated.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Ferrari_cdn||12-27-2001||05:16 PM||||I usually have the same problem.  I can't seem to find the solution yet.  When very cold, it will run at 2000 smoothly.  But after a while it will slowly drop until it drops below 1500 then it will drop really fast to like 500.  The motor will kick itself back to 1500 and stay there, doing the cycle maybe a few times then stay at 1500.  I think my motor is realizing it can't idle at 900 smoothly because it will flutcate (sp?) so it tries to warm up at 1500 for awhile.<P>When its cold, it doesn't like to accelerate fast.  It will hesitate, then shoot forward.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ICEFierosig.gif">  AIM: CanadianFiero<p>[This message has been edited by Ferrari_cdn (edited 12-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Lizzy||12-27-2001||07:41 PM||||My problem isn't with the fast idle at warm up. While the motor is cold, and i give it some throttle, say to 2500rpms it will not hold there.  It falls off to 2000rpms, then back up to 2500 about every two seconds, back and forth.||||reg||1
